From 9b7ecf435a3cafdc84b47ab9f6cc379f54700f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:21:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the update on the device, the matrix-free diagonal and
 the failures in the Newton correction

- update and revert of a behaviour integrated on the device: the material
  properties, the external state variables and the mass density are updated
  on the host (mgis::behaviour::updateInputValues), as on the host, and the
  arrays are synchronized on the host for reading afterwards, so that the
  host copies stay valid after an update or a revert;
- NewtonSolver::computeNewtonCorrection: an exception thrown by the tangent
  operator, its diagonal or its action is registered in the context of the
  resolution, which fails, instead of reaching std::terminate;
- MatrixFreeTangentOperator::AssembleDiagonal: |P^T| diag(A) on
  non-conforming meshes, as mfem::BilinearForm::AssembleDiagonal;
- the constrained matrix-free operator keeps a copy of the essential
  degrees of freedom, and is rebuilt when they change;
- JacobiSmoother: the list of essential degrees of freedom referenced by
  the smoother of MFEM is a member, and the smoother is kept between
  operators of the same size;
- addStiffnessMatricesDiagonals: thread count checked per node;
- raiseOnFailureOnAnyProcess (MPI.hxx) and getFiniteElementSpace
  (FiniteElementDiscretization.hxx) shared instead of copied;
  TangentOperatorComputation read once into an enumeration;
- documentation of the synchronizations updated;
- BatchIntegrationTest: behaviour with a thermal expansion whose
  temperature varies in time (IsotropicLinearHardeningThermoPlasticity),
  states read on the host without synchronization after each update and
  revert, diagonal of the matrix-free operator compared to the assembled
  one, matrix-free operator refused with a boundary integrator.
---
